{
  "module": "Attention: how tokens exchange information",
  "lesson": {
    "slug": "multi-head",
    "title": "Multi-head attention",
    "summary": "Why attention is run as several heads in parallel, how the heads are split and joined, and how many parameters the layer has.",
    "covers": ["multi-head-attention", "mha-parameter-count"],
    "prerequisites": [
      {
        "lesson": "attention-output",
        "reason": "A head is one attention computation like the one just described."
      },
      {
        "lesson": "sequence-shapes",
        "reason": "The heads split d_model, so the shape notation must already be readable."
      }
    ]
  },
  "screens": [
    {
      "ref": "one-head-limit",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "One attention computation produces a single set of weights for each position. But a position may need to attend to different tokens for "
            },
            {
              "text": "different reasons",
              "bold": true
            },
            {
              "text": ", all at once."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "A single softmax head would have to "
            },
            {
              "text": "average",
              "bold": true
            },
            {
              "text": " those different patterns into one distribution."
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "sources": [
        {
          "title": "Transformers in LLMs: mechanics and pipeline (flashkarte deck, cards 39)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "ref": "several-heads",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "The solution is "
            },
            {
              "text": "h heads",
              "bold": true
            },
            {
              "text": " running in parallel. Each head has its "
            },
            {
              "text": "own",
              "bold": true
            },
            {
              "text": " W_Q, W_K and W_V, which project d_model "
            },
            {
              "text": "down",
              "bold": true
            },
            {
              "text": " to a smaller size:"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "formula",
          "latex": "d_k = d_v = d_{\\mathrm{model}} / h",
          "spoken": "d k equals d v equals d model divided by h"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "In the original paper, h = 8 and d_model = 512, so each head works with d_k = 512 / 8 = 64."
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "sources": [
        {
          "title": "Transformers in LLMs: mechanics and pipeline (flashkarte deck, cards 38)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "ref": "join",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "Each head produces an output of shape n × d_v. The h outputs are "
            },
            {
              "text": "concatenated",
              "bold": true
            },
            {
              "text": " side by side, giving n × (h · d_v) = n × d_model, and then multiplied by an output matrix W_O of shape d_model × d_model:"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "formula",
          "latex": "\\mathrm{MultiHead}(X) = \\mathrm{Concat}(\\mathrm{head}_1, \\ldots, \\mathrm{head}_h)\\, W_O",
          "spoken": "Multi-head of X equals the concatenation of head 1 up to head h, times W O"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "The result has the same shape as the input, n × d_model."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "tone": "note",
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "Implementations usually do one big projection for all heads and then reshape it into heads. The result is the same."
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "sources": [
        {
          "title": "Transformers in LLMs: mechanics and pipeline (flashkarte deck, cards 38)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "ref": "why-several",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "Each head can learn a "
            },
            {
              "text": "different attention pattern",
              "bold": true
            },
            {
              "text": ", looking for a different kind of relation in a different subspace, all in parallel."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "It also costs about the same as one full-width head, because each head works in the reduced size d_model / h."
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "sources": [
        {
          "title": "Transformers in LLMs: mechanics and pipeline (flashkarte deck, cards 39)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "ref": "parameters",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "How many parameters does the layer have? W_Q, W_K, W_V and W_O are each d_model × d_model when all the heads are counted together, so:"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "formula",
          "latex": "4\\, d_{\\mathrm{model}}^{2}",
          "spoken": "four times d model squared"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "For d_model = 768 that is 4 × 768² = 2,359,296, about 2.36 million. For d_model = 512 it is 4 × 512² = 1,048,576. (Biases are ignored.)"
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "sources": [
        {
          "title": "Transformers in LLMs: mechanics and pipeline (flashkarte deck, cards 40)"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "questions": [
    {
      "prompt": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "The model has d_model = 512 and h = 8 heads. What is d_k for each head?"
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "options": [
        {
          "correct": true,
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "spans": [
                {
                  "text": "64"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "reason": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "spans": [
                {
                  "text": "d_k = d_model / h = 512 / 8."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "correct": false,
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "spans": [
                {
                  "text": "512"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "reason": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "spans": [
                {
                  "text": "That is d_model, the full width."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "correct": false,
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "spans": [
                {
                  "text": "4,096"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "reason": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "spans": [
                {
                  "text": "That is 512 × 8. The heads split d_model, they do not multiply it."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "correct": false,
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "spans": [
                {
                  "text": "8"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "reason": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "spans": [
                {
                  "text": "That is the number of heads."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "teaches": ["several-heads"],
      "covers": ["multi-head-attention"],
      "variants": [
        {
